From: mojito-mainline <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: use an identity domain for the SM6150 MDSS

The bootloader leaves the display scanning out of its splash buffer through
the SMMU stream. Without an identity default domain the display stream is
switched to an empty translation context at boot: every fetch faults
(hundreds of thousands per second), the panel goes black and the DSI video
engine underflows, so the panel driver cannot send its init sequence.
Add qcom,sm6150-mdss to the list that already covers sm6115, sm6350, sm8150.

Signed-off-by: mojito-mainline <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c	2026-11-26 12:36:59.717615046 +0500
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c	2026-11-26 12:36:59.738562258 +0500
@@ -421,6 +421,7 @@
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdm845-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sdm845-mss-pil" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6115-mdss" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6150-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6350-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6375-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8150-mdss" },
